Rewritten: the whole tool on Nodecode's own seams. The two observer hooks
(pre_api_request, pre_auxiliary_call) became one hook on the round point and one
on the credential point; the ledger is one tab-separated metadata line per
request in this home's data folder, and the CREDENTIAL hook is what names the
host a request went to. The config audit reads ~/.nodecode/config.jsonc instead
of Hermes's config and prints Nodecode's own `(config-set ...)` form as the fix;
`/xray fix <id> yes` writes through the same code the config panel uses. The
canary, the read-only store search with masked snippets and the self-contained
HTML leak map are the original's, over this home's files.

Left out, and why: the German translation (Nodecode speaks one language here);
the optional guard middleware that masked canary and watch values in outgoing
text, which needs an intercepted request body this harness does not hand a cell;
the dashboard tab (its own web page); the SQLite queries into Hermes's state.db
(replaced by a byte search over this home's files, so no schema is assumed); the
ledger rotation keeps one older file rather than parsing JSONL; and the
`--deep` pass and the access report of the subject finder, which were queries
against Hermes's stores only. Nothing in the original was a network call, and
nothing in this rewrite is one either.
